{
 "description": "Which space a world-unit falloff's metric is evaluated in when the edited layer carries a non-identity item transform. The two self-consistent readings are: (a) LAYER-LOCAL -- the vertex is compared against the falloff handles exactly as both are stored, so the region of influence stretches with the layer and becomes an ellipsoid in world; (b) WORLD -- the vertex is lifted by the layer's item matrix first and the handles are world coordinates, so the region stays a sphere in world and looks squashed in the layer's own units. Each case below predicts different weights under the two readings; `weights` is the measured answer and `weightsIfLayerLocal` is the reading the measurement rejected.",
 "task": "0644",
 "capturedBy": "committed translate under a falloff, weight recovered from the per-vertex displacement as w = d . T / |T|^2 with T taken from the falloff-free control of the same item transform; every displacement was verified parallel to T (largest off-axis residual 4.0e-8)",
